From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8917: use APCS mailbox for RPM

The legacy qcom,ipc path creates a syscon regmap for APCS and acquires
its first clock, the CPU PLL. Without the PLL provider, RPM SMD setup
defers before its clock and regulator services can become available.
Simply enabling the PLL provider also lets syscon accesses gate that
clock, which is not appropriate for a minimal boot relying on firmware's
CPU clock configuration.

Use the APCS mailbox driver, as the other SMD edges already do. Channel
0 writes bit 0 at offset 8 for the existing MSM8939 APCS compatible,
preserving the legacy IPC signal without attaching the CPU PLL to the
register accesses.

Base: pem120/linux-msm89x7 a51b91b503307d35902447dd1f90db765372cf3b
Assisted-by: LLM

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8917.dtsi
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@
 
 		smd-edge {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 168 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
-			qcom,ipc = <&apcs 8 0>;
+			mboxes = <&apcs 0>;
 			qcom,smd-edge = <15>;
 
 			rpm_requests: rpm-requests {
